    {
      "source": "HOKFIRE",
      "url": "https://www.hokfire.com/",
      "field": "guide",
      "content": {
        "pros": [
          "Built-in shield",
          "Strong anti CC Ultimate",
          "Good mobility"
        ],
        "cons": [
          "Can be kited",
          "Vulnerable to disengage",
          "Damage isn't instant"
        ],
        "gameplay_tips": "## Early Game\nIn the early game, Devara can use his ranged attacks to punish the enemy when they want to walk up and last-hit minions. When looking to trade, always use Skill 1 Thunderblaze to gain a shield and an empowered auto attack to win every time. Always use a skill when at full energy. Do not waste the downtime of stacking your passive with auto attacks. Even if you use Skill 1 to get an empowered auto attack to help clear the wave or jungle camp, it all helps his tempo.\n\n## Teamfights\nIn teamfights, as Devara, you need to play patiently. You don't want to be the first hero that goes in. You want to use your range and mobility to kite in fights and poke the enemy. Use your Ultimate when you are about to get hit by crowd control or need to escape; however, be careful because you can still take damage and die whilst transforming. After being transformed, you can look to play aggressively with his bonus damage and quick passive stacking.\n\n## Tips & Tricks\nAlways auto-attack after using a Skill to deal extra magic damage and restore health\nSkill 1 can be used to dash over walls\nStack your passive on minions or monsters before trading or joining a teamfight"
      }
    },
    {
      "source": "Kurohiko",
      "url": "https://hok.kurohiko.id/",
      "field": "tactical_tips",
      "content": "Cooldown transformasi Devara lama banget. Incer dia di jeda abis dia berubah."
    },
